Mathematics acts as a wonderful bridge across diverse cultures, 
an idea clear to us when discussing Euler's famous formula $e^{i\pi} + 1 = 0$; 
a scholar from China named it 欧拉公式 in their native tongue, 
while our Burmese classmate smiled, adding "ဒါက အလွန်အရေးကြီးတဲ့ တွက်ချက်မှုဖြစ်တယ်" 
to note its immense value in complex calculations.
